## Development Environment

This project uses [devbox](https://www.jetify.com/devbox) to manage the dev environment.

```bash
devbox shell        # enter the dev environment
devbox run dev      # go run ./cmd/{{ project_name }} (port {{ port }})
devbox run test     # go test -race -cover ./...
devbox run quality  # golangci-lint + go build gate
```

Canonical `devbox run` scripts (configured in `devbox.json`):

| Script | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `dev` | `go run ./cmd/{{ project_name }}` |
| `test` | `go test -race -cover ./...` |
| `test-fast` | `go test ./...` |
| `lint` | `golangci-lint run` (vet, staticcheck, gosec, errcheck, gocritic, revive, …; see `.golangci.yml`) |
| `lint-fix` | `gofmt -w . && goimports -w . && golangci-lint run --fix` |
| `typecheck` | `go build ./...` |
| `quality` | `lint` then `typecheck` — the gate CI runs |
| `audit` | `govulncheck ./...` |
| `secrets-scan` | detect-secrets against `.secrets.baseline.json` |
| `security` | `audit` + `secrets-scan` |
| `image-build` | Build local image `{{ project_name }}:scan` |
| `image-scan` | trivy against `{{ project_name }}:scan` |

**Rule for every agent (human, CI, and AI): never call `go`, `gofmt`, `goimports`, `golangci-lint`, `govulncheck`, `detect-secrets`, or `trivy` directly. Always go through `devbox run <script>`. Adding a dependency: `devbox run -- go get <module>` then `devbox run -- go mod tidy`.**

## Claude Code agents

Agents and slash commands come from the [`ika100/sdlc-foundry`](https://github.com/ika100/sdlc-foundry) marketplace, enabled in `.claude/settings.json`:

- `svc-go@sdlc-foundry` — Go coder, tester, deployment, observability, release agents
- `svc@sdlc-foundry` — orchestrators (`/svc:*`), product-manager, architect
- `shared@sdlc-foundry` — quality, security, `/shared:check-quality`, `/shared:new-service`

### Common workflows

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Plan a feature, no code (first step) | `/svc:plan-feature <description>` |
| Build the approved plan | `/svc:build-feature --plan docs/plan/<slug>.md` |
| Small change | `/svc:quick-task <description>` |
| Fix a bug | `/svc:fix-bug <description or error>` |
| Read-only quality + security audit | `/shared:check-quality` |
| Release | `/svc:release` |

### Spec first

A feature starts with a spec, not code: run `/svc:plan-feature <description>`, review the stories in `docs/backlog.md` and the plan in `docs/plan/<slug>.md`, then build it with `/svc:build-feature --plan docs/plan/<slug>.md`. The PR cites the story ids (`STORY-NNN`). Small changes (`/svc:quick-task`) and bug fixes (`/svc:fix-bug`) are exempt.

## Feature Branch Workflow

Branch prefixes: `feature/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `docs/`, `refactor/`, `release/`. Slugs: lowercase, hyphens, ≤40 chars. Main is protected; all changes via PR. Required CI checks: `quality`, `test`, `security`, `pr-title`, `docker`. PR titles follow Conventional Commits (`type(scope): description ≤72 chars`).

## Module layout and conventions

```
cmd/{{ project_name }}/main.go   entrypoint: config, slog JSON logger, graceful shutdown; `Version` set via ldflags
internal/config/                 environment-based configuration
internal/server/                 chi router, handlers, middleware{% if needs_observability %} (metrics.go: Prometheus){% endif %}
```

- **Router:** `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5`; handlers are plain `http.Handler`/`http.HandlerFunc`, middleware is `func(http.Handler) http.Handler`. No bespoke context types.
- **Logging:** stdlib `log/slog` (`slog.JSONHandler`); pass `*slog.Logger` explicitly, structured key/values, never log secrets.
- **Config:** environment variables only (see `docs/env-vars.md`).
- **Probes:** `GET /health` and `GET /ready` must keep responding.
{%- if needs_observability %}
- **Metrics:** `GET /metrics` (Prometheus `client_golang`); request counter/latency are recorded by the `instrument` middleware, labelled by chi route pattern.
{%- endif %}
- **Errors:** wrap with `fmt.Errorf("…: %w", err)`; no panics for control flow.
- **Tests:** stdlib `testing` next to the code (`*_test.go`), table-driven where it helps; `httptest` for handlers. `testify` only if requested.
- **Version:** never hardcode; it comes from the git tag via `-ldflags "-X main.Version=…"` (ADR-012).
- **Docs:** plans in `docs/plan/`, ADRs in `docs/adr/`, backlog in `docs/backlog.md`.

## Docker image pipeline

CI's `docker` job builds the static binary into `gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` (no shell; probes are Kubernetes-side) and pushes on `main` (`latest`, `sha-<short>`) and on `v*.*.*` tags (semver tags; the tag is passed as `VERSION` build arg). Registry: `{{ docker_registry }}/{{ project_name }}`.

## Deployment

This repo ships **only a container image**. Kubernetes manifests, environment wiring (e.g. `API_URL`), replicas, resources and exposure belong to the product's `gitops-app` repo (platform ADR-017): register the service with `/gitops:compose add {{ project_name }}` (needs the GitHub topic `deployable-service`, set by `/shared:new-service`), then `/gitops:promote {{ project_name }} <from> <to>`. Change how the service runs by editing its entry in that repo's `services.yaml`; change the port, probe paths or user in the Dockerfile/app and update the entry to match.
